---
<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 3.4 · Slayer Backbone, Monkey Madness II & Theatre" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="3-4" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 3.4</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Slayer Backbone, Monkey Madness II &amp; Theatre</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Train Slayer between quests, gathering useful runes and cash along the way. After Monkey Madness II and A Night at the Theatre, use their combat rewards to help finish 75 Magic.</p>
      </header>
      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Check cash and runes → Crafting 70 → Slayer 65 → Land of the Goblins → Slayer 69 → Grand Tree balloon + Monkey Madness II → Slayer 74 → A Night at the Theatre → claim six combat rewards → finish Magic 75."
        stats={["70 Crafting and 69 Slayer for Monkey Madness II", "74 Slayer for The Blood Moon Rises later", "75 Magic for Dragon Slayer II and Desert Treasure II; use quest rewards first"]}
        unlocks={["Royal seed pod, demonic gorillas and maniacal monkeys", "Land of the Goblins and A Night at the Theatre complete", "No fixed cash stack, black mask, Bowfa or rare crossbow required"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>Train Slayer before spending the combat rewards.</strong> Save Duke's rewards and the Theatre's lamps until the Slayer sessions below are complete. Bursting a suitable task can earn Magic XP while its drops help pay for runes. Once you finish Slayer, check how much XP you still need for 75 Magic and use the rewards where they help most.</div>
      <section><div class="section-label">Supplies · prepare for the next task</div><h2>Check your coins and runes before buying more.</h2></section>
      <div class="callout"><strong>Check your bank:</strong> coins; items to alch and nature runes; chaos, death, water, fire and air runes; any blood/soul runes; Prayer-restoring potions and food; glass, gems and battlestaff materials; and any black mask, Slayer helmet or rune crossbow you already have. Check your Slayer points too. Keep enough coins for quest items, food, travel and emergencies. Buy combat runes for the next task or a small batch, then use the drops and remaining supplies to decide whether to buy more.</div>
      <p><strong>Where the battlestaff money went:</strong> the 1,590 Earth battlestaves in Chapter 2.1 gave an estimated <strong>1,590 × 2,300 = 3,657,000 coins</strong> above the staff purchase cost, before rune costs and shop-price variation. Much of that paid for later steps: roughly <strong>550,000–612,500 coins</strong> for the first oak/teak planks, potentially <strong>500,000–750,000 more</strong> for 70 Construction at 500 coins per additional teak plank, 200,000 for Iban's staff, 130,000 for Barrows gloves, 125,000 for the camphor hull, 25,000 for Proselyte and roughly <strong>188,000 for the gold leaf and basic rooms</strong>. Those purchases total about <strong>1.72–2.03m</strong>. After Royal Trouble, the kingdom can also use <strong>75,000 coins per day</strong>: <strong>25 days × 75,000 = 1.875m</strong>, bringing that example to <strong>3.59–3.91m</strong> before other quests, supplies or new income. Depositing coins in the coffer sets that money aside for its daily use. Your balance depends on your plank needs, kingdom days and extra income, so check both your bank and coffer. If coins are tight, reduce or pause kingdom top-ups while keeping enough for quests and supplies. <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-1/`}>2.1 budget</a> · <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-3/`}>kingdom draw</a> · <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-6/`}>later planks</a>.</p>
      <div class="callout"><strong>If cash is low:</strong> earn enough for a small rune batch while keeping money for quest items, food and travel. It is reasonable to have only a few hundred thousand coins left after Chapter 2's purchases. Alch useful drops you already have, using banked nature runes where possible, or choose a money-making method below. Check the coins received before buying combat runes.</div>
      <ExpandableNote title="Ways to earn more cash, from relaxed to active" label="Choose a method if needed">
        <p><strong>Choose what suits you:</strong> Fortis wealthy citizens for low attention; the Agility Pyramid for predictable coins; Hallowed Sepulchre Floor 3 for active play and Magic supplies; Giants' Foundry for spare metal and Smithing XP; or Ardougne Knights for familiar, more click-heavy pickpocketing. You can start these without a particular cash stack, a Rogue outfit or a long Agility session.</p>
        <p><strong>Relaxed default — Stealing valuables, Civitas illa Fortis:</strong> Children of the Sun and 50 Thieving are already cleared. At the Bazaar, wait for a street urchin to distract a wealthy citizen, then click that citizen; the roughly 20-second automatic pickpocket window succeeds without repeated clicks and can give a house key. Use keys on the currently vacant wealthy-citizen houses, loot their valuables, and leave through the window when warned that the owner is returning. Sell valuables to <strong>Oriana outside the Fortis west bank</strong>. The published combined method is around <strong>140k GP/hour with Rogue equipment and Gladiator rank</strong>; your rate will depend on whether you have those bonuses and how actively you play. Ordinary burglary itself is more like <strong>90k–125k coins/hour</strong> during efficient house-looting time, with the combined cash rate varying with keys and attention; the burglary portion can give roughly <strong>70k–105k Thieving XP/hour</strong>. Already-owned Rogue equipment improves key acquisition, but do not grind for it just to start. Choose this if you want a lower-attention session while watching something. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Stealing_valuables" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Stealing valuables loop</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Stealing_valuables" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Published rate assumptions</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Predictable coins — Agility Pyramid:</strong> travel to the pyramid in the Kharidian Desert, bring waterskins or other heat protection, climb to the top, pick up the pyramid top and give it to <strong>Simon Templeton for 10,000 coins</strong>; repeat. Ordinary runs are around <strong>200k GP/hour</strong>, approaching <strong>260k/hour</strong> with clean laps at sufficiently high Agility. At 69+ Agility only the jump gaps can fail, and at 75 the course becomes fail-proof. You can start with your current level; training to 75 is optional. Unlike loot-value estimates, each completed lap pays predictable liquid GP without expensive inputs or drop RNG. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Agility_Pyramid" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Pyramid route and rate</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Active option with useful supplies — Hallowed Sepulchre:</strong> Sins of the Father is done. Enter near Darkmeyer and run its timed obstacle floors; Floors 1/2/3 ask for 52/62/72 Agility. The <strong>August 2026 update made floor entry boostable</strong>, so unboosted 70 Agility plus an ordinary <strong>+3 Agility potion</strong> opens Floor 3 without training base 72. Rush Floors 1 and 2, learn the obstacle timing, take the worthwhile Floor-3 coffin opportunities and repeat instead of looting everything. Published practiced Floor-3 estimates are roughly <strong>640k–665k GP/hour in total loot value</strong>, <em>not liquid coins/hour</em> or a guaranteed Ironman sale price. Coins, alchable rune gear, death/nature/blood/soul/law/cosmic/elemental runes, Prayer potions and ranarr supplies can directly refill this chapter's Magic and Slayer budget. Choose this when you feel like practising obstacles while collecting useful supplies. <a href="https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/summer-sweep-up---agility--chambers-of-xeric-changes?oldschool=1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official boosted-entry update</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Hallowed_Sepulchre_(Floor_3)" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Floor-3 loot assumptions</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Convert banked metal — Giants' Foundry:</strong> if the bank has spare steel, mithril, adamant bars or suitable equipment, take them to the already-unlocked Foundry south-east of Al Kharid and make commission swords: fill the crucible with the chosen metal, select a mould, then work each temperature/tool stage for direct coins and Smithing XP. Optimised reward-coin examples span roughly <strong>180k–400k GP/hour</strong>, but starter moulds, mistakes and the available alloy can lower that, and buying costly metal changes net profit. Keep the metal needed for quests, Ranged ammunition and Sailing, and use only the spare stock. Foundry training also helps toward the 72 Smithing needed for The Blood Moon Rises later. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Giants%27_Foundry" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Foundry start and loop</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Giants%27_foundry/Strategies" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Alloys and rates</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Familiar alternative — Ardougne Knights:</strong> pickpocket the Knights in East Ardougne for repeatable coins and Thieving XP if you prefer a simple, more click-heavy method. The often-quoted <strong>270k–280k GP/hour</strong> Ironman figures assume roughly 95+ Thieving, Ardougne Medium diary and full Rogue equipment; at a lower level or without those bonuses, expect less. Choose Knights if you enjoy their straightforward routine. Wear your Rogue outfit to double pickpocket loot if you have it available. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Ironman_money_making_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Optimised Ironman rate assumptions</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>When to stop:</strong> return to Slayer or Magic when your coins and banked runes cover the next batch, with money left for quests, food and travel. For a suitable Ancient-Magic task, roughly <strong>200–500 casts</strong> is a useful starting batch. Check your remaining runes and task drops afterward; buy more as needed throughout the 65→74 Slayer training.</p>
      </ExpandableNote>
      <ExpandableNote title="Why BRUHsailer's Chapter 3 cash number does not transfer" label="Source-route comparison">
        <p><a href="https://umkyzn.github.io/BRUHsailer/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current BRUHsailer</a> reaches roughly <strong>35.8m GP, 93 Magic and 59 Slayer</strong> around Chapter 3 after training toward 98 Agility with Hallowed Sepulchre/Fletchpalchre and alching along the way. You skipped that long session in this guide, so you will likely have less cash and Magic XP. Its later goals also include 100 combat, roughly 75 Slayer, 92 Ranged and the Corrupted Gauntlet. Here, buy runes as you need them and use the quest rewards according to your own levels.</p>
      </ExpandableNote>

      <section><div class="section-label">Prepare for Monkey Madness II</div><h2>Reach the Crafting and Slayer levels the quest needs.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i34-crafting-70" number="1" title="Reach 70 Crafting for Monkey Madness II">
        <p>The Fremennik Exiles awarded <strong>50,000 Crafting XP</strong>. If you entered it at exactly level 65, <strong>449,428 + 50,000 = 499,428 XP</strong>; level 70 starts at <strong>737,627</strong>, leaving at most <strong>238,199 XP</strong>. Check your current XP and use banked glass, gems or remaining orb/staff materials to work toward 70. You can make fresh glass from sand and soda ash at a furnace. <strong>Superglass Make needs 77 Magic</strong>, so use the furnace if you are below that level. Gather or buy enough materials for the XP you still need.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="A cash-light alternative: Wyrmscraig Golem Crafting" label="Alternative Crafting method">
          <p>After Fallen From Grace, sail or use its unlocked Wyrmscraig travel to <strong>Auchrie on Wyrmscraig</strong> and go to the nearby sunstone mine/golem plinths. Bring a pickaxe, hammer and chisel. Mine <strong>five sunstones per golem</strong>: four start the base at an empty plinth, while the fifth is chiselled into its core. Shape the four sides, then insert the core and one suitable Hunter fur; the finished golem yields Crafting XP and an uncut gem. Wyrmscraig goat fur can be hunted on the island, so rare furs or cash purchases are not prerequisites. The quieter loop uses the sunstone monolith and normal shaping clicks; moving between individual rocks for momentum and clicking to speed shaping is the active alternative. A goat-fur golem gives about <strong>2,440 Crafting XP</strong>, so a 238,199-XP gap would take about <strong>98 golems</strong> before any XP from cutting gems or other Crafting. Check your XP and stop sooner if you reach 70. It trades gathering time for minimal GP expense. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Golem_crafting" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current activity and material guide</a>.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p>Use whichever material bank and pace suit you. <strong>Stop at an unboosted 70 Crafting.</strong></p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i34-slayer-65" number="2" title="Reach 65 Slayer and unlock dust devils">
        <p>If you finished Exiles with <strong>323,742 Slayer XP</strong>, level 65's <strong>449,428 XP</strong> is at most <strong>125,686 XP</strong> away; any extra tasks have already shortened that. Take ordinary assignments from a master you can use at your combat level. Your dragon scimitar/defender, Fire Cape, Piety, Barrows gloves and defensive/prayer gear work for melee tasks; the Arkan blade is useful in some situations. Bank alchables, runes, herbs and useful supplies. Wear a black mask or Slayer helmet if you have one, and leave Cave Horror sessions optional. <strong>Stop at 65 Slayer.</strong></p>
        <ExpandableNote title="When should I mage a Slayer task?" label="Optional method decision">
          <p><strong>Dust devils unlock at 65 Slayer.</strong> On a naturally assigned task, the multicombat <strong>Catacombs of Kourend</strong> are the non-Wilderness default: buy/wear a <strong>facemask from a Slayer equipment shop</strong> unless an already-owned Slayer helmet protects you, gather/stack the devils, keep Prayer and health under control, and burst the stack. At 67+ Magic, <strong>Smoke Burst</strong> is available (<strong>4 chaos, 2 death, 2 air, 2 fire</strong> per cast); at 70 Magic, <strong>Ice Burst</strong> is the stronger ordinary choice (<strong>4 chaos, 2 death, 4 water</strong> per cast). Shadow Burst and Blood Burst cost more for this routine, while Blood's healing can be situational. A first <strong>200-cast batch</strong> is at most 800 chaos and 400 death runes, plus the matching elemental runes; count banked stock before buying. Alch/keep the drops; dust-devil loot often offsets much of the supply bill, but task and drop RNG make net profit unguaranteed. Melee ordinary single-target tasks; burst other naturally assigned, stackable multi-target tasks when practical. Do not spend a large Slayer-point balance forcing dust devils, Wilderness-burst by default, or burn Ancient runes on a task where their area damage gains little. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Dust_devil" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Dust-devil protection/locations</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Slayer_task/Dust_devils" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Task methods</a>.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i34-land-goblins" number="3" title="Quest break: complete Land of the Goblins">
        <p>Talk to <strong>Grubfoot at the Dorgesh-Kaan mine entrance</strong>, then escort him to Zanik/Oldak in the city. Earlier chapters covered Another Slice of H.A.M., Fishing Contest and the Agility, Fishing, Thieving and Herblore requirements. Check your bank for a safe light source, <strong>toadflax potion (unf), goblin mail (several pieces), yellow/blue/orange/purple dyes</strong>, an empty vial and pestle for black-mushroom dye, fishing rod, <strong>one raw slimy eel and five coins</strong>. If the potion (unf) is missing, obtain one toadflax from the <strong>Brimhaven Agility Arena voucher shop</strong> as in 2.4 (three vouchers), then mix it with a vial of water. Keep this unfinished potion for the quest. For a missing <strong>raw slimy eel</strong>, take a fishing rod, bait, a <strong>lit enclosed light source</strong> and tinderbox into the <strong>Lumbridge Swamp Caves</strong>. With The Lost Tribe complete, enter via the Lumbridge Castle cellar passage; bring antipoison for the cave hazards and catch one at a cave fishing spot with 28 Fishing. Bank it <strong>raw</strong>, not cooked. Goblin mail and the black mushroom can be obtained during the quest. Bring a fairy-ring staff, Dorgesh-Kaan spheres/teleports, and ordinary combat gear/food for the temple encounters; bank between the Dorgesh-Kaan, Goblin Village and Goblin Cave/temple phases rather than carrying every disguise at once. Clear inventory/equipment when the goblin transformation requires it; do not bring a following pet into the temple. Claim <strong>8,000 XP each in Agility, Fishing, Thieving and Herblore</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Lumbridge_Swamp_Caves" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cave access and hazards</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Land_of_the_Goblins" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest items and phases</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Buy the dyes; collect the disguise mail inside the temple" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Buy <strong>two yellow, two blue and two red dyes from Oronwen in Lletya</strong>, already accessible after Song of the Elves. Keep one yellow and one blue dye; combine one red + one yellow for orange, and the other red + blue for purple. This makes the four colours needed; check your bank for spare dyes before buying them.</p>
          <p>The <strong>crate immediately east inside the goblin temple, beyond the entrance guards</strong>, supplies unlimited goblin mail. Take the pieces needed for the black, white, yellow, blue, orange and purple disguises there. Pick a <strong>black mushroom in the Goblin Cave</strong> and crush it with a pestle and mortar while holding <strong>one empty vial</strong> for black dye. The whitefish/white-mail phase uses the <strong>raw slimy eel, fishing rod and five coins</strong>; keep the eel uncooked.</p>
          <p>Buy missing fishing rod and bait from <strong>Gerrant in Port Sarim</strong>, and the vial and pestle from <strong>Jatix in Taverley</strong>. Obtain only the missing <strong>one toadflax</strong> through the voucher recovery above, mix it with one vial of water, and keep it unfinished for the goblin potion. If the dark-cave kit is missing, use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-1/#i31-wgs`}>retained lantern or its recovery recipe</a> and the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>antipoison supply</a>.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p>This is a current Quest Cape quest and a breather from Slayer. <strong>Hopespear's Will is a separate, optional miniquest</strong>, not a required continuation here.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i34-slayer-69" number="4" title="Continue from 65 to 69 Slayer before Monkey Madness II">
        <p>Level 65 starts at <strong>449,428 XP</strong> and 69 at <strong>668,051 XP</strong>, a difference of <strong>218,623 XP</strong>. Complete ordinary tasks and check your coins and runes between them. Burst suitable assignments—Smoke Burst before Magic 70, Ice Burst afterward—and use melee for single targets. You can take tasks as they come instead of spending points to seek dust devils. <strong>Stop at an unboosted 69 Slayer</strong> and claim Monkey Madness II's 80,000 Slayer XP before returning to tasks.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Grandmaster quest · phased preparation</div><h2>Unlock the balloon destination, then finish Monkey Madness II.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i34-mm2" number="5" title="Verify the Grand Tree balloon route and complete Monkey Madness II">
        <p><strong>Check the balloon destination:</strong> you need the <strong>Gnome Stronghold/Grand Tree route unlocked</strong> before starting Monkey Madness II, as well as Enlightened Journey. If it is still locked, bank weapons and armour, take <strong>three magic logs</strong> to the Entrana balloon and unlock the destination with your <strong>60 Firemaking</strong>. Check your bank for the logs first. If short, collect the missing logs from <strong>Movario's one-time WGS treasure room</strong>; the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-1/#i31-wgs`}>WGS instructions</a> explain how to reach its 100 magic logs. This avoids waiting for Wintertodt drops or trying for a +5 stew boost. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Balloon_transport_system" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Balloon unlocks</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Find the three magic logs and gather the quest items" label="Quest preparation">
          <p><strong>Three logs, only if the destination is locked:</strong> after delivering Movario's notes to Thaerisk, use the tunnel in the south-west corner of his study to reach the WGS treasure room. Take the missing magic logs and bank them; they are unnoted. If you already used the entire one-time cache, you can cut more at <strong>75 Woodcutting</strong>. A brown-spice stew boost may let you cut them at a lower base level if you want to try, but both the boost and time to receive logs vary. Stop when you have the three logs needed.</p>
          <p>Buy <strong>one lemon and one grapes from Heckel Funch in the Grand Tree</strong>, a pestle and mortar from Jatix if missing, and cut <strong>one ordinary log</strong> for the Entrana travel phase. Reclaim the translation book from Narnode. Bank weapons and armour before Entrana. Keep <strong>20 coins</strong> for Gu'Tanoth if you use its normal approach rather than the unlocked shortcut.</p>
          <p>Before Ape Atoll, check the <strong>M'speak amulet and ninja monkey greegree</strong> retained from Monkey Madness I / RFD. If either is missing, use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-2/#i22-monkey-madness`}>M'speak amulet replacement recipe</a> and <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-4/#i24-awowogei`}>ninja greegree recovery</a> before starting the island phase. A separate <strong>monkey talisman</strong> for Kruk's greegree costs <strong>1,000 coins at Tutab's Magical Market on Ape Atoll</strong> if absent; the ninja greegree is not consumed to replace that talisman. The laboratory's crates supply a missing <strong>hammer and chisel</strong>. Keep a lit lantern, pickaxe and slash weapon for the relevant dungeon route, and prepare <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>Prayer potions, antipoison and ordinary energy potions</a> before entering; stamina is only an already-owned convenience.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>Requirements:</strong> unboosted <strong>69 Slayer, 70 Crafting, 60 Hunter, 55 Agility, 55 Thieving and 60 Firemaking</strong>, plus Enlightened Journey <em>and its Gnome route</em>, The Eyes of Glouphrie, RFD Freeing King Awowogei/Monkey Madness I, Troll Stronghold and Watchtower. The previous chapters cover the quest chain and other levels. Start with <strong>King Narnode in the Grand Tree</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Monkey_Madness_II/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current phase/item guide</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Stage the story items:</strong> first a <strong>lemon, grapes, pestle and mortar, translation book</strong> (reclaim from Narnode if lost), and ordinary logs for Entrana; leave weapons/armour in the bank for that visit. On Ape Atoll, take the <strong>M'speak amulet, ninja monkey greegree, monkey talisman and light source</strong>, plus anti-poison, food and a one-click exit. The dangerous Kruk dungeon has an Agility route with failures into aggressive monkeys, or a tanking route needing a <strong>pickaxe and slash weapon</strong>. Unlock its return shortcut, then bank/regear for Kruk; take his paw to Zooknock for a Kruk greegree. Later phases revisit Kob at Troll Stronghold and Keef at Gu'Tanoth (bring 20 coins for the normal approach), then use the quest's satchels in the airship/laboratory. Follow the linked map for individual obstacles; do not carry every phase's inventory at once.</p>
        <p><strong>Combat equipment:</strong> melee with dragon scimitar (Arkan only where suitable), dragon defender, Fire Cape, Barrows gloves, Piety and normal defensive gear. Range with the Chapter 3.3 <strong>adamant crossbow or an already-owned RCB</strong>, remaining plain/enchanted bolts, Ava's accumulator and banked d'hide. Bring food, Prayer restores, poison cures, energy/stamina if available and a teleport. For <strong>Kruk</strong>, Protect from Missiles against his hard ranged hit and range/kite or carefully flinch from the wall; maintain a safe health margin because his melee still hurts. <strong>Kob/Keef</strong> hit hard even through prayer: use the matching protection, move, eat and regear between them. In the lab, clear the required <strong>tortured gorillas</strong>, then the <strong>two mandatory demonic gorillas</strong> by watching their protection prayers and attack styles, switching between your melee and Ranged equipment. After those two fights, continue the quest; returning for a zenyte is optional.</p>
        <p><strong>Glough's three rooms:</strong> use the door/hallway to range his melee-only first phase. Lure the second phase back toward the first room's wall for the documented ranged safespot. <strong>Restock before entering the third phase</strong>; it can hit extremely hard and pull you into melee distance. With your crossbow, keep high HP, Protect from Magic at range (Melee when forced adjacent), fire a controlled shot, then move back toward the previous chamber; repeat rather than tanking repeated pulls. A slower hit-and-retreat flinch can be learned from the linked strategy if supplies are low. If you already own a weapon with a 10-square attack range, the linked guide describes an optional advanced safespot. Leaving or dying during Glough resets his phases; instanced unprotected items go to a grave outside, and items dropped on the floor are lost. Do not treat quest death as a safe minigame death. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Monkey_Madness_II" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Glough phases, death and rewards</a>.</p>
        <p>Claim the <strong>fixed 80,000 Slayer, 60,000 Agility, 50,000 Thieving and 50,000 Hunter XP</strong>, plus the reusable <strong>Royal seed pod</strong> and new gorilla/maniacal-monkey access. If you entered at exactly 69 Slayer, <strong>668,051 + 80,000 = 748,051 XP</strong>, already past level 70's <strong>737,627 XP</strong>. Check your Slayer XP afterward. <strong>Leave Duke's two selectable 50,000-combat-XP rewards unclaimed</strong> until after the next Slayer block and Theatre. Duke's choices are Attack, Strength, Defence, Hitpoints, Ranged or Magic—<strong>not Slayer</strong>. A black mask, whip, zenyte, Bowfa, crystal armour, blowpipe or RCB drop remains optional.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i34-slayer-74" number="6" title="Reach 74 Slayer after Monkey Madness II">
        <p><strong>The Blood Moon Rises needs an unboosted 74 Slayer later.</strong> After Monkey Madness II, you need at most <strong>1,096,278 − 748,051 = 348,227 Slayer XP</strong>; check your current XP to see how much remains. Continue ordinary tasks, bursting suitable multicombat assignments and using melee on single targets. Bank alchables, coins, runes, herbs and other useful supplies as you go. You can reach the goal with the tasks and equipment available to you. <strong>Stop at 74 Slayer.</strong></p>
        <p><strong>After the last task:</strong> check your Magic XP, coins, alchables, chaos/death/elemental/blood/soul runes, Prayer-restoring potions and food. Bursting may have brought you closer to 75 Magic; if you mostly used melee, the quest rewards and methods below cover the remaining training.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Quest break · learn the Theatre</div><h2>Complete the current story, then Entry Mode.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i34-night-theatre" number="7" title="Complete A Night at the Theatre after Slayer 74">
        <p><strong>Complete the investigation before entering the Theatre.</strong> With A Taste of Hope already complete, talk to the <strong>Mysterious Stranger at Ver Sinhaza</strong>; use Drakan's medallion and bank between investigations. Bring the retained <strong>Ivandis or blisterwood flail, saw, ghostspeak amulet and an axe</strong>. Investigate Ranis Drakan's grave, kill the required vyrewatch, inspect the spider-egg cave without attempting to kill its high-Slayer araxytes, carry antipoison for venom and leave the cave safely. Then visit <strong>Filliman at the Nature Grotto</strong> (fairy ring BIP), cross the swamp to the quest Hespori and fight it with food, antipoison and your ordinary combat kit. A druid pouch protects food from ghasts. Chop the defeated plant for bark and return to the Stranger; you are then ready for the Theatre. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/A_Night_at_the_Theatre" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current reworked quest</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Replace quest tools and make the poison weapon before Entry Mode" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>If the flail is missing, buy a <strong>replacement blisterwood flail for 40,000 coins from Ivan Strom</strong> in the Myreque hideout beneath Old Man Ral's house in Meiyerditch; Sins of the Father is already complete. Reclaim the <strong>ghostspeak amulet from Father Urhney</strong> in Lumbridge Swamp. A sawmill operator sells a saw, and Bob in Lumbridge sells a basic axe; there is no rare tool requirement.</p>
          <p>For the poisoned dagger described below, set aside <strong>one clean kwuarm, one vial of water and one ground blue dragon scale</strong>. Mix the kwuarm potion (unf), then add the dust to make ordinary weapon poison at 60 Herblore and apply it to the dagger. If no kwuarm remains, kill <strong>ordinary chaos druids in Taverley Dungeon</strong> until the missing herb drops; clean it and stop at one. The blue-dragon-area scale is a repeatable ground spawn, so no dragon kill or scale drop is required.</p>
          <p>Buy <strong>insulated boots from a Slayer equipment shop</strong> if Arrav's pair is missing. Refill <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>Prayer potions and ordinary antipoison</a> before the investigations and raid. With ordinary antipoison, one dose reduces venom to poison and a second cures that poison; avoid another application while escaping the spider cave. The quest supplies its strange eggs, acid and Hespori bark; a Farming seed or normal Hespori kill is unnecessary.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>Entry Mode</strong> at Ver Sinhaza is substantially gentler than normal Theatre and allows unlimited room retries; it is a learning run, not a unique-item farm. Take three attack styles: scimitar/defender/Fire Cape and a <strong>poisoned dragon dagger</strong> or other poison weapon, the adamant crossbow or banked RCB/Ava/d'hide, and an affordable Magic spell/runes. If no poisoned dagger is banked, buy a plain dragon dagger from <strong>Jukat's shop in Zanaris</strong> (Lost City is complete) and apply <strong>weapon poison</strong>. Jukat is inside the marketplace, which requires <strong>one spare cut diamond for entry</strong>: check the bank after the 3.3 enchanted-bolt uses, and if none remains mine Shilo Village gem rocks until a diamond appears and cut it at the route's Crafting level. Do not spend a diamond reserved for needed bolt tips; bring coins for the dagger separately. Actual 70 Herblore can make the basic poison from a kwuarm potion (unf) and dragon scale dust if none is banked. For missing dust, collect <strong>blue dragon scales from the repeatable ground spawns in the Taverley blue-dragon area</strong> (the route's 70 Agility opens the shortcut; take dragonfire protection), then grind them with a pestle and mortar. Bring food, Prayer restores, poison cure and <strong>insulated boots for solo Verzik</strong>. Entry supply chests offer bandages after Bloat and Sotetseg; these heal and restore/boost resources, and failures give further supplies. Take what each room needs rather than treating a failed attempt as a reason to buy raid gear. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Theatre_of_Blood/Entry_Mode" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Entry equipment, supplies and room mechanics</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Six-room primer:</strong> at <strong>Maiden</strong>, Protect from Magic and move off blood pools. At <strong>Bloat</strong>, use pillars/line of sight, move with him and attack only during safe downtime. At <strong>Nylocas</strong>, match grey/melee, green/Ranged and blue/Magic, protect the pillars, and do not keep attacking a spider with the wrong style. At <strong>Sotetseg</strong>, react to prayer-colored attacks and follow the revealed maze path. At <strong>Xarpus</strong>, move off poison, manage the poison phase, then avoid attacking when he turns to stare. At <strong>Verzik</strong>, use the provided <strong>Dawnbringer</strong> for phase one, move between pillar cover and attack windows, then manage bombs/electric ball (solo insulated boots), kill the <strong>purple healing Nylocas with poison</strong>, and adapt prayers/movement as phases change. Use the linked room guide to learn each encounter's patterns.</p>
        <p><strong>Death rules:</strong> Entry Mode's 2023 changes removed its 100,000-coin reclaim fee and allow unlimited retries, but deaths are <strong>dangerous for Hardcore Ironman and Hardcore Group Ironman status</strong>. Ordinary accounts may retry, but should still reclaim items promptly before another unsafe death. Check the death rules for your account type before entering. After finishing the Entry run, return to the Stranger and complete the quest. Its four <strong>20,000-combat-XP lamps</strong> are held for Step 8. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Item_Retrieval_Service" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Entry reclaim fee</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Theatre_of_Blood" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Hardcore death rule</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Quest rewards · finish 75 Magic</div><h2>Choose your reward skills after checking your Magic XP.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i34-magic-75" number="8" title="Claim the six combat rewards and finish 75 Magic">
        <p><strong>Check your Magic XP, coins and runes before choosing.</strong> Duke offers <strong>2 × 50,000</strong> combat XP, and A Night at the Theatre gives <strong>4 × 20,000</strong> lamps: <strong>180,000 XP total</strong> across six rewards. You can choose Attack, Strength, Defence, Hitpoints, Ranged or Magic; <strong>Slayer is not eligible</strong>. If Magic is already 75+, put the rewards into <strong>Strength</strong>, or another eligible combat skill you would rather improve. If Magic is below 75, use the 20k lamps first for a small gap. Use one or both 50k rewards on Magic if they would save a useful amount of rune spending and training; put the remaining rewards into Strength by default. Claim all six, checking the updated XP after each choice. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Monkey_Madness_II" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Duke reward</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/A_Night_at_the_Theatre" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Theatre lamps</a>.</p>
        <p>After claiming the rewards, subtract your current Magic XP from <strong>1,210,421</strong> to find how much remains to level 75. If you are already there, this step is complete. Otherwise, choose a method below to finish the unboosted 75 Magic needed for Dragon Slayer II and Desert Treasure II.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Existing alchables:</strong> High Alch useful banked/Slayer drops with banked nature runes on the standard spellbook. This converts existing stock to liquid coins and Magic XP; do not manufacture an arbitrary mountain of alchables.</li>
          <li><strong>Cheap and quieter:</strong> after The Heart of Darkness, reach <strong>Frost Crabs in the Ruins of Tapoyauik</strong> and autocast Fire Bolt with the Family Crest <strong>chaos gauntlets</strong>. These low-danger crabs have <strong>−50 Magic Defence and 100% Fire weakness</strong>, making Fire Bolt substantially stronger here than on a neutral crab; they stay aggressive for roughly ten minutes before you reset their aggression. Each cast uses <strong>one chaos, four fire and three air runes</strong>; a fire staff removes the fire-rune input. Gauntlets raise the ordinary base max hit from 12 to 15 before the target's weakness applies. This is the recommended low-attention Magic method. Buy runes in small batches and check your XP before restocking. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Frost_Crab" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Frost Crab properties</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Fire_Bolt" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Spell and runes</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Fast, cash-sensitive:</strong> after MM2, maniacal monkeys in <strong>Kruk's Dungeon</strong> stack densely and drop one-dose Prayer potions. Protect from Melee, gather a stack and Ice Burst at 70+ Magic. Around <strong>1,000 casts/hour</strong> consumes about <strong>4,000 chaos, 2,000 death and 4,000 water runes/hour</strong>; at a rough 800–1,000 GP-equivalent per cast that is <strong>~0.8–1.0m rune value/hour</strong> before shop-price variation. Plan around <strong>~200k Magic XP/hour</strong> with ordinary gear and Ice Burst's 22 base max hit; stronger Magic-damage gear can reach the low/mid-200s and near 280k. Try a small batch with your own equipment to judge the XP and rune use, then stop at 75 Magic. Ice Burst is sufficient here; Barrage spells are optional. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Maniacal_monkey/Strategies" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Monkey method and damage tiers</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Ice_Burst" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Spell runes</a>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Stop at an unboosted 75 Magic.</strong> You are ready for the coming quests.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">3.4 complete · Slayer and Magic ready</div>
        <h3>Take your Royal seed pod and quest experience into the next chapter.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Skills:</strong> unboosted 70+ Crafting, 74+ Slayer and 75+ Magic.</li>
          <li><strong>Quests/unlocks:</strong> Land of the Goblins, Grand Tree balloon destination, Monkey Madness II and A Night at the Theatre complete; Royal seed pod and gorilla/maniacal-monkey access obtained; fixed MM2 80k Slayer XP claimed.</li>
          <li><strong>Rewards:</strong> Duke's two 50k rewards and the Theatre's four 20k lamps claimed in the skills you chose.</li>
          <li><strong>Keep ready:</strong> Fire Cape, crossbow and remaining bolts, plus the coins and runes left after training. Black mask/Slayer helmet, whip, zenytes, gorilla uniques, RCB, Bowfa/crystal, blowpipe, Rigour and Ava's assembler remain optional upgrades.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
